   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the village of Kings Point, town of North Hempstead, county\nof Nassau, to alienate and discontinue certain parklands for the purpose of\nproviding additional parking for the community center being built by the\nUnited Mashadi Jewish Community of America, and to replace such alienated\nparkland with a new, dedicated parkland",
    "basePrintNo": "S7868",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7868-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Kings Point, Village of",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7868\n\nSPONSOR: MARTINS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act authorizing the village of Kings Point, town of North Hempstead,\ncounty of Nassau, to alienate and discontinue certain parklands for the\npurpose of providing additional parking for the community center being\nbuilt by the United Mashadi Jewish Community of America, and to replace\nsuch alienated parkland with a new, dedicated parkland\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill seeks to alienate and discontinue parklands to provide addi-\ntional parking and to replace such alienated parkland with a new dedi-\ncated parkland.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 allows the village of Kings Point, acting by and through its\ngoverning body to discontinue parklands and alienate the lands described\nin section three of this act for the purpose of providing additional\nparking for the community center being built by the United Mashadi\nJewish Community of America.  Section 2 states that the authorization\nprovided shall be effective only upon the condition that the village of\nKings Point dedicates the lands described in section four of this act as\nparkland. Section 3 states that the parklands authorized by section one\nof this act to be alienated consist of 2.4817 acres as described.\nSection 4 states that prior to the discontinuation and alienation of the\nparkland described in section three, the village of Kings Point shall\ndedicate as parkland such land consisting of 5.76 acres as described.\nSection 5 states that if the fair market value of the parklands escribed\nin section four are not equal or greater that the fair market value of\nthe parklands to be alienated as described in section three, the village\nof Kings Point shall dedicate the difference of the fair market value of\nthe land for the acquisition of additional parklands and/or capital\nimprovements to existing park and recreational facilities. Section 6\nstates in the event that the village of Kings Point received any funding\nsupport or assistance from the federal government for the purchase,\nmaintenance or improvement of the parklands set forth in section three\nof this act, the discontinuance and alienation of such parkland author-\nized by the provisions of this act shall not occur until the village of\nKings Point has complied with any federal requirements pertaining to the\nalienation or conversion of parklands.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Great Neck Park District administers and maintains the parkland on\nbehalf of the Village of Kings Point. Such park district has requested\nthat the Village of Kings Point consent to a land swap. This will enable\nthe Village to afford the public with superior park facilities that are\nbeing lost by the alienation.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
